   = note: proven from the static cost model, for every size from 1 up
   = note: the cost is that of the optimized program (spec "Performance contracts")

tests/ui/check/ok_cost_proven.sky:14:12: note: `A⁻¹ @ b` is rewritten to a Cholesky solve
   |
14 |     return A⁻¹ @ b
   |            ^^^^^^^
   |            - positive definite
   = note: rewrite `A⁻¹ @ b` to a Cholesky solve: A is Matrix[N,N] and PositiveDefinite, b is Vector[N]. Factor A = L·Lᵀ (L lower-triangular), solve L·y = b, then Lᵀ·x = y. x = A⁻¹·b is Vector[N], and A⁻¹ is never formed.

